## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-region ordering, coordination, failover recovery, and durable state management in a realistic KCNA-like system.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant global sequence
- Cross-region coordination
- Durable storage and idempotent processing
- Reordering buffers for in-order emission
- Failure/recovery paths and testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal sketch
class Coordinator {
  constructor(store) { this.store = store; }
  allocate(tenantId) {
    const last = this.store[tenantId]?.lastSeq || 0;
    const next = last + 1;
    this.store[tenantId] = { lastSeq: next };
    return next;
  }
  commit(tenantId, seq) {
    // durable commit placeholder
    this.store[tenantId].lastSeq = Math.max(this.store[tenantId].lastSeq, seq);
  }
}
class Consumer {
  constructor(coord) { this.coord = coord; this.buff = new Map(); }
  onMessage(msg) {
    const { tenantId, globalSeq } = msg.meta;
    if (!this.buff.has(tenantId)) this.buff.set(tenantId, new Map());
    const map = this.buff.get(tenantId);
    map.set(globalSeq, msg);
    this.flush(tenantId);
  }
  flush(tenantId) {
    const map = this.buff.get(tenantId);
    let seq = this.coord.peekNext(tenantId);
    while (map.has(seq)) {
      const m = map.get(seq);
      // process(m)
      map.delete(seq);
      seq++;
      this.coord.commit(tenantId, seq);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle clock skew and coordinator failover?
- What metrics would you surface for latency and duplicates?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of schema versioning, dead-letter routing, and offset discipline in KCNA.

## Key Concepts

- Versioned in-memory JSON schema registry
- Payload validation with a JSON schema validator
- Dead-letter routing to invalid_events
- Offset management and at-least-once semantics
- Lightweight deduplication for idempotence

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton illustrating onMessage flow
function onMessage(msg) {
  const payload = JSON.parse(msg.value);
  const version = payload.schemaVersion;
  const schema = registry.get(msg.topic + '|' + version);
  if (!schema) { publishInvalid(msg, 'Unknown schemaVersion'); return; }
  if (!validate(payload, schema)) { publishInvalid(msg, 'Validation failed'); return; }
  publishMain(msg);
  commitOffsets(msg);
}
```

