## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a scalable, privacy-preserving per-tenant DP aggregator in a streaming KCNA pipeline, including budget accounting, isolation, and test strategy for real-world fleet telemetry.

## Key Concepts
- Differential privacy in streaming; per-tenant budgeting; windowing; sensitivity; noise distribution; composition.
- Data model: tenant-id, vehicle readings, hourly windows, sums/counted values.
- System design: sandboxed operators, per-tenant isolation, watermarking, backpressure, fault tolerance.
- Testing: DP correctness, privacy accounting, performance under burst, end-to-end latency.

## Code Example
```javascript
function laplace(scale) {
  const u = Math.random() - 0.5;
  return -scale * Math.sign(u) * Math.log(1 - 2 * Math.abs(u));
}
function addDpNoise(sum, count, epsilon) {
  const noisySum = sum + laplace(1 / epsilon);
  const noisyCount = count + Math.max(1, Math.round(laplace(1 / epsilon)));
  return noisySum / Math.max(1, noisyCount);
}
``` 

