## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical stateful streaming concepts: windowed aggregations, per-tenant isolation, watermark-based late data handling, and exactly-once guarantees across rebalances. It also tests testing discipline and observability planning.

## Key Concepts

- Stateful windowed aggregations with per-(tenantId, userId) keys
- Watermarks and late-arrival handling (120s)
- Reb alo nce-safe state partitioning and eviction
- Exactly-once or idempotent sinks with proper offsets
- Observability and test strategy for late data and rebalancing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: window state store and onEvent flow
class WindowAggregator {
  constructor(windowMs, watermarkMs) { /* init stores */ }
  onEvent(e) {
    // e = {tenantId, userId, ts, value}
    const ws = Math.floor(e.ts / this.windowMs) * this.windowMs;
    const key = `${e.tenantId}:${e.userId}:${ws}`;
    let bucket = this.state.get(key) || {sum: 0, count: 0, maxTs: 0};
    bucket.sum += e.value;
    bucket.count += 1;
    bucket.maxTs = Math.max(bucket.maxTs, e.ts);
    this.state.set(key, bucket);
    // emit when window closes or on a timer
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle out-of-order data beyond the watermark?
- How would you design compensation if the sink fails mid-replay?
- What metrics would you expose for latency, throughput, and backpressure?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a beginner KCNA candidate's ability to implement a time-window join across topics, with late data, offset handling, and at-least-once guarantees. It requires simple in-memory state management, per-key routing, and clear API boundaries.

## Key Concepts

- Time-window joins across topics
- Late-arriving data handling
- Per-message offset tracking
- Idempotent emissions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch for in-memory join
class JoinEnricher {
  constructor() {
    this.latestAnnotation = new Map(); // serviceId -> { annotation, ts }
    this.metricBuffer = new Map(); // serviceId -> [{metric, ts}]
  }
  processMetric(metric, offset, ts) {
    const ann = this.latestAnnotation.get(metric.serviceId);
    const enriched = ann ? { ...metric, annotation: ann.annotation } : { ...metric, annotation: null };
    this.emitEnriched(enriched, offset);
  }
  processAnnotation(ann, offset, ts) {
    this.latestAnnotation.set(ann.serviceId, { annotation: ann.value, ts });
    // re-emit any buffered metrics for this service
    const buffered = this.metricBuffer.get(ann.serviceId) || [];
    for (const m of buffered) {
      this.emitEnriched({ ...m.metric, annotation: ann.value }, m.offset);
    }
    this.metricBuffer.set(ann.serviceId, []);
  }
  emitEnriched(record, offset) {
    // send to metrics_enriched and commit offset afterward
  }
}
```

